 "description": "One video: what happens in it, its beats, its numbers and its formats. By a post's link or Shorti's video_id: what happens in it, its hook, turn and beats (Shorti's reading), its `cues` where a director read it (the moments worth copying, each with what to do and what its drawing points at, `look_at`), the director's `checklist` in the order one shoots, `to_shoot` (what it takes to shoot it again: `needs` in Shorti's words \u2014 how many people, where, how the camera is held, with what, how much editing \u2014 its closed `codes`, and where the asked language has them the `props`, the `camera` set-ups and what the presenter `does`), views and views per day, length, its page and the formats it belongs to. A video Shorti has not read answers `not_in_corpus`. The default detail='summary' is the compact reading; detail='full' answers every compiled field (large). The previous detail='brief' remains accepted.",
 "inputSchema": {
  "additionalProperties": false,
  "properties": {
   "detail": {
    "default": "summary",
    "description": "summary: compact agent answer, Korean person-facing text with lang=ko; model prompts are marked for_model=true. full: all compiled details, including original bilingual/model text.",
    "enum": [
     "summary",
     "full"
    ],
    "type": "string"
   },
   "lang": {
    "default": "ko",
    "description": "The creator's language. 'en' answers in the English Shorti wrote: never translate its Korean yourself.",
    "enum": [
     "ko",
     "en"
    ],
    "type": "string"
   },
   "url": {
    "anyOf": [
     {
      "maxLength": 2048,
